<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<xmile version="1.0" level="3" xmlns="http://www.systemdynamics.org/XMILE" xmlns:isee="http://iseesystems.com/XMILE">
    <header>
        <smile version="1.0" namespace="std, isee">
            <uses_arrays>1</uses_arrays>
        </smile>
        <name>stage4.v5</name>
        <uuid>55cc9693-4ed3-4627-a52c-c50f777ffa4d</uuid>
        <vendor>isee systems, inc.</vendor>
        <product version="10.1.2" isee:saved_by_v1="false" lang="en">iThink</product>
    </header>
    <style>
        <model font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
        <interface font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
    </style>
    <sim_specs method="Euler" time_units="sec" isee:pause_after_rates="false" isee:instantaneous_flows="false">
        <start>0</start>
        <stop>6</stop>
        <dt>0.005</dt>
        <isee:analyze_mode>false</isee:analyze_mode>
    </sim_specs>
    <dimensions>
        <dim name="Dim_Name_1" size="1" />
    </dimensions>
    <model_units />
    <isee:sensi_specs run="false" runs="5">
        <method>multivariate</method>
        <isee:variable max="1.8" min="0.2" type="incremental" name="Initial_water_vol">
            <num_samples>5</num_samples>
        </isee:variable>
    </isee:sensi_specs>
    <isee:prefs last_model="true" layer="model" grid_width="20" grid_height="50" divide_by_zero_alert="true" link_high_level_map="true" show_module_prefix="true">
        <isee:window width="630" height="428" />
        <isee:security />
        <isee:print_setup width="576" height="756" />
    </isee:prefs>
    <isee:equation_prefs order_by="sector" />
    <model>
        <stock name="Displacement">
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <inflow>Veloc</inflow>
            <display x="199" y="48" color="blue" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Veloc">
            <doc>The &quot;If...then&quot; switch turns velocity off when the rocket hits the ground.</doc>
            <eqn>IF(Displacement&lt;= 0 and Velocity &lt;= 0) THEN(0) ELSE(Velocity)</eqn>
            <display x="128" y="48" color="blue">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="78" y="48" />
                    <pt x="179" y="48" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <stock name="Velocity">
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <scale min="-35" max="35" />
            <inflow>Acceleration</inflow>
            <display x="204" y="111" color="blue">
                <scale min="-35" max="35" />
            </display>
        </stock>
        <flow name="Acceleration">
            <doc>The &quot;if...then&quot; switch turns the acceleration off when the rocket hits the ground.</doc>
            <eqn>IF(Displacement &lt;=0 and Velocity&lt;0 )THEN(0) ELSE(Total_force/(Mass_of_water+Empty_rocket_mass))</eqn>
            <display x="135" y="116" color="blue">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="87" y="116" />
                    <pt x="184" y="116" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="Air_resistance">
            <eqn>c2*Velocity^2</eqn>
            <display x="294" y="118" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Total_force">
            <eqn>if Velocity &gt;= 0 then Thrust-Weight-Air_resistance else Thrust- Weight+Air_resistance</eqn>
            <display x="200" y="180" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Weight">
            <eqn>(Mass_of_water+Empty_rocket_mass)*Gravity</eqn>
            <display x="205" y="234" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Gravity">
            <eqn>9.8</eqn>
            <display x="248" y="246" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Empty_rocket_mass">
            <eqn>.2</eqn>
            <display x="132" y="197" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <stock name="Volume_of_water">
            <eqn>Initial_water_vol</eqn>
            <outflow>Rate_of_water_loss</outflow>
            <display x="145" y="309" color="blue" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Rate_of_water_loss">
            <eqn>Flow_through_orifice</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="200" y="308" color="blue">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="165" y="308" />
                    <pt x="235" y="308" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="Thrust">
            <eqn>if Pressure_difference &gt;=0  OR Volume_of_water&gt;= 0 then (Cross_sectional_area_of_hole*Pressure_difference) else 0</eqn>
            <display x="351" y="221" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Atm_pressure_in_psi">
            <eqn>14.7</eqn>
            <display x="210" y="379" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Density_of_air">
            <eqn>1</eqn>
            <display x="395" y="22" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Volume_empty_rocket">
            <eqn>2</eqn>
            <display x="51" y="412" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Rocket_pressure">
            <doc>In this equation the initial pressure is multiplied by the ratio of the initial air volume to the current air volume.  This is an applicaton of Boyle&apos;s Law.  The pressure changes in inverse proportion to the  change in volume.  The MAX function is there to prevent the pressure in the bottle from dropping below atmospheric pressure. </doc>
            <eqn>If Volume_of_water &gt;=0 then MAX((Initial_pressure+Atm_pressure)*(Volume_empty_rocket-Initial_water_vol)/(Volume_empty_rocket-Volume_of_water),Atm_pressure) else Atm_pressure</eqn>
            <display x="121" y="395" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Initial_pressure">
            <doc>Metric conversion</doc>
            <eqn>Initial_pressure_in_psi*6900</eqn>
            <display x="116" y="441" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Atm_pressure">
            <doc>metric conversion</doc>
            <eqn>Atm_pressure_in_psi*6900</eqn>
            <display x="261" y="421" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="c2">
            <eqn>Factor_for_air_resistance* (Density_of_air*Cross_sectional_area_of_rocket)/4</eqn>
            <display x="332" y="66" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Cross_sectional_area_of_rocket">
            <eqn>(PI*(Rocket_diameter)^2)/4</eqn>
            <display x="402" y="76" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Rocket_diameter">
            <eqn>.1</eqn>
            <display x="419" y="122" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Initial_pressure_in_psi">
            <doc>Guage pressure</doc>
            <eqn>70</eqn>
            <display x="60" y="456" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Initial_water_vol">
            <eqn>1</eqn>
            <display x="65" y="360" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Density_of_water">
            <eqn>1</eqn>
            <display x="48" y="289" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Pressure_difference">
            <eqn>Rocket_pressure-Atm_pressure</eqn>
            <display x="349" y="421" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Mass_of_water">
            <eqn>Volume_of_water/Density_of_water</eqn>
            <display x="62" y="220" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Factor_for_air_resistance">
            <doc>This factor relates to nose cone and rocket shapes.</doc>
            <eqn>1</eqn>
            <display x="291" y="18" color="blue" label_angle="277" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Flow_through_orifice">
            <doc>This equation for a flow rate through an orifice comes from Mark&apos;s Engineering Handbook, Sixth Edition, McGraw-Hill, p 3-62</doc>
            <eqn>1000*.61*Cross_sectional_area_of_hole*(2*Gravity*Equivalent_pressure_head)^.5</eqn>
            <display x="271" y="337" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Cross_sectional_area_of_hole">
            <eqn>.00034</eqn>
            <display x="338" y="286" color="blue" label_angle="248" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Equivalent_pressure_head">
            <doc>Atmospheric pressure will support a column of water 10.3 meters tall.  This formula calculates the equivalent head in the pressurized bottle.</doc>
            <eqn>10.3*Pressure_difference/Atm_pressure</eqn>
            <display x="326" y="365" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <display page_width="576" page_height="756" isee:converter_size="large" interval="0.05">
            <connector x="71" y="370" uid="0">
                <from>Initial_water_vol</from>
                <to>Rocket_pressure</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="126" y="406" uid="1">
                <from>Rocket_pressure</from>
                <to>Pressure_difference</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="182" y="107" uid="2">
                <from>Velocity</from>
                <to>Veloc</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="71" y="227" uid="3">
                <from>Mass_of_water</from>
                <to>Weight</to>
            </connector>
